<p>The empty struct has a size of zero. Since its alignment is 1, it can exist at any address, because every number is divisible by 1.</p>

<p>Interestingly, its stride is 1. This is because even though <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">EmptyStruct</code> has a size of zero, every <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">EmptyStruct</code> you create must have a unique memory address.</p>

