    <span class="p">}</span>
  <span class="p">}</span>
<span class="p">}</span>

</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>This prints the raw bytes of the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">SampleStruct</code> instance.</p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">withUnsafeBytes(of:)</code> gives you access to an <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UnsafeRawBufferPointer</code> that you can use inside the closure.</p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">withUnsafeBytes</code> can also be used as an instance method on <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Array</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Data</code>.</p>

<h3 id="computing-a-checksum">Computing a Checksum</h3>

<p>Using <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">withUnsafeBytes(of:)</code>, you can return a result. For example, you can use it to compute a 32-bit checksum of the bytes in a struct.</p>

<p>Add the following code to your Playground:</p>

<div class="language-swift highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><!-- <td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
2
3
4
