</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Never bind memory to two unrelated types at the same time. This is called <strong>type punning</strong>, and Swift doesn’t like puns. :]</p>

<p>Instead, use methods like <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">withMemoryRebound(to:capacity:)</code> to temporarily rebind memory.</p>

<p>Additionally, rebinding from a trivial type (like <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Int</code>) to a non-trivial type (like a class) is illegal. Don’t do it.</p>

